The Planck units are an exercise in dimensional analysis. They represent the scale at which
gravitational and quantum effects are naively expected to converge under the assumption that
$G$ is relevant to electromagnetism. The Tetryonic framework suggests this assumption is
false at the level of planar wave propagation.

