\section{Conclusion}
% ================================================================

This paper presents a structured conjecture, not a proof. The Vacuum Frequency Theory
proposes that the speed of light $c$ is not merely a propagation velocity but a geometric
counting rate: the number of invariant equilateral gauge bosons of physical height
$\lq = 10^{-15}$\,m that pass a fixed point per second in a perfect vacuum.

The zero-point mass $\mz$, derived independently from Carbon-12 geometry, recovers
Planck's constant exactly when multiplied by $c^{2}$. The equilateral triangle is the unique
geometry consistent with planar tessellation, the Pythagorean law, and the dimensional
structure of Planck's action. All electromagnetic quanta are integer multiples of the
invariant gauge area $\Aq$.

The open problem is stated precisely: prove or disprove that $\lq = 10^{-15}$\,m is the
unique electromagnetic gauge cutoff. Until this is resolved in either direction, the framework
